From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] d3d10umd: a device starts with the framebuffer for no views

A new device's framebuffer state was all zeroes, never sent: a draw before the first SetRenderTargets (stream output
only, no render target, as a GPU simulation's first pass can be) ran on a GL framebuffer without attachments or size,
which is incomplete (GL_INVALID_FRAMEBUFFER_OPERATION): nothing was written, and the DrawAuto that read it next lost
the context. The device now starts with the framebuffer SetRenderTargets makes for no views (D3D's largest size).
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/Device.cpp b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/Device.cpp
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/Device.cpp
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/Device.cpp
@@ -182,6 +182,12 @@
    pipe->bind_vs_state(pipe, pDevice->empty_vs);
    pipe->bind_fs_state(pipe, pDevice->empty_fs);
 
+   /* No views bound yet: the framebuffer SetRenderTargets makes for none (a draw before any, e.g. stream output
+    * only, finds GL's framebuffer complete) */
+   pDevice->fb.width = pDevice->fb.height = 16384;
+   pDevice->fb.layers = 1;
+   pipe->set_framebuffer_state(pipe, &pDevice->fb);
+
    pDevice->max_dual_source_render_targets =
          screen->get_param(screen, PIPE_CAP_MAX_DUAL_SOURCE_RENDER_TARGETS);
 
